          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "cuda-unit (ci/sections.yml, the job that runs on the yoga runner with a device) derives the cuda-only test set as the cuda --list minus the default --list (comm -23, line 3298), runs that set by name with --exact and no --ignored (line 3311), requires passed + ignored to equal the derived count (3317), and fails on any line matching a device-skip pattern that includes CUDA model init failed (3323). K1 is in the cuda-only set (its module is cfg(feature = \"cuda\")), so cuda-unit still runs it, on a device, and the panic text is caught twice: by cargo exiting non-zero first, and by the device-skip grep if it ever reached it. mutants-cuda derives its set the same way (line 3420), so a mutant that breaks CUDA init now fails K1 instead of surviving it."
          },
          "properties": {
