          "ruleId": "fit_check_need_ignores_serve_batched_slots",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Carried from the previous receipt, source unchanged at head (gguf/cuda/mod.rs is byte-identical to the previously receipted head; the only file the new commit touches is the K1 test). The QK-norm fit check in build() computes need = weights + cache + reserve + kv_per_pos * max_seq_len for both modes; for FitServing the KV length was sized against 1 + SERVE_BATCH_SLOTS slots, so need counts one slot. fit_batched_kv_alloc shrinks the batched slots to what fits rather than failing."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Read of build() and session_kv::serving_kv_len at head, carried from the previous receipt where it was raised independently by the primary and by the antigravity reviewer; not measured on a device. The antigravity reviewer did not raise it again this run (its two findings are about the K1 change).",
            "failure_scenario": "A QK-norm model on a card where serving_kv_len hits its 4096 floor keeps the FP16 batched prefill cache, and the later batched-KV allocation gets fewer than SERVE_BATCH_SLOTS slots (a throughput loss logged as X1-KVALLOC), or in the worst case a CUDA OOM at batched init.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
